  "summary": "Seven preprints push spatial transcriptomics toward 3D subcellular embeddings, deconvolution, clonal mapping and live-tissue sampling, with tumour annotation and isoform work alongside.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is increasing resolution and information content in spatially resolved expression. Computational work spans a rotation-equivariant network learning 3D transcript embeddings from subcellular data, st2sc inferring single-cell profiles from multicellular spots, SpOTr mapping tumour clones to spots via phylogeny-aware Fused Gromov-Wasserstein optimal transport, and SpaceMACE adding spatial proximity to tumour-cell annotation. Experimentally, LIFE-seq and LANCE-seq sample living tissue repeatedly with nanoforest and encoded microneedle arrays, enabling longitudinal tracking of cortical injury and APAP-induced liver injury within the same animals. FULL-seq, though not spatial in the summary, jointly profiles chromatin accessibility and full-length transcripts per cell to link promoter regulation to alternative first exon usage. Together these shift the field from static snapshots toward temporal, clonal and isoform-aware spatial inference.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
